A||||11||fropuff||Gas Mileage?||||6||
Z||000000||fropuff||04-19-2000||09:22 AM||||Hey, I was wondering what the average gas mileage is for an 86 GT automatic.  I filled it up on Saturday, says about 40 miles on the trip meter.  My gas gauge says it's about 9/16 of a tank full.  This means I should get 100 miles to the tank; 10 miles to the gallon.  What's right...my trip meter or my gas gauge?  Thanks.||||reg||6
Z||000001||olympic||04-19-2000||01:17 PM||||    You really can't judge gas mileage from only driving 40 miles and by looking at the gas gauge.  The only real way to do it is to reset the trip meter and fill up the tank.  Then drive the car as you normally would for 500 or more miles while keeping track of all the fuel you put in.  At the end, fill the tank and total up the fuel used and divide the total amount of fuel used by total miles travelled.<BR>   This will give you a good average of what mileage you are getting.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||04-19-2000||11:49 PM||||Don't be surprised if that is close to your actual mileage! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I read posts that guys with v-6's saying they were only getting between 11mpg - 18mpg around town. I scoffed big and loud 'cause I have a Coupe (4 cyl) that gets 36 mpg hwy! Now I own an '87 GT 5 spd. Should be the most economical 6 cyl tranny combo there is...No performance mods other than K&N and 165 deg thermostat. So far I am getting around 21mpg from what I can tell. But that gas needle sure drops quick on this thirsty lil' pig compared to the Coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||04-20-2000||12:56 AM||||We've had this discussion before (check archives), but some of us with V6 5 speeds get around 20 mpg in town and about 30 cruising on the open road.   <P>I would expect the automatic to get 2-5 mpg less because of gear ratios. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierodave||04-20-2000||05:32 AM||||Fierodave 86 GT 410 4-speed  just checked this last tank today  24.8 MPG <BR>all around (Fun) driveing!! And I don't live in the city :~) And yes, I was supprized too! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||04-20-2000||09:09 AM||||Last fall I went on a 2,200 mile trip.  I got 23.3 at 80mph on the interstate and 27.7 on backroads at night at 50-55mph (looking for deer).  A week ago I adjusted my TPS and went on a 600 mile trip (combination of 80mph interstate and 70mph sideroad driving) and got 25mpg average.||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||04-20-2000||02:56 PM||||My '87 GT automatic gets 26.9 to 27 on the hwy and around 15 in town....||||reg||6
Z||000007||ChadMan||04-20-2000||03:05 PM||||When I borrowed my father-in-law's 86 SE automatic for 6 weeks, I got about 190-200 miles per tank driving in town and 220-230 driving on the highway.  It had 65K miles at the time and was (is) in a flawless state of tune.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||04-21-2000||08:52 PM||||I got 29 MPG with my Formula on the highway with a few full throttle tests when I first got it (@68 mph cruise) and 24.3 MPG around town a few months later with leaking exhaust manifolds, which causes bad gas mileage. Not bad for a gas-guzzler, huh! <P>I forgot to say I have a five speed.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Racer 1||04-22-2000||12:48 AM||||My 2.5 Duck drinks about 1 gallon per 16 miles highway and about 12 miles to da gallon in town. My fiero has over 208,000 on da DUCK!||||reg||6
Z||000010||William Federle||04-22-2000||11:45 AM||||I drive 100 miles / day round trip to work and I fill up every other day. My 1984 duck gets 29 - 30 MPG.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||04-23-2000||04:16 AM||||My 86 GT 5 speed gets about 12 mpg around town..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  but I've hit 26 mpg on a 70mph highway run.  <P>front exhaust manifold crack, and lots of full throttle runs don't help around town mileage..  my 84 sport coupe gets around 20mpg in town and 27-30 mpg on highway||||reg||1
